      sources: "Sources: Learn, Resource Graph samples for Service Health; impacted resources; Subscription vs tenant events; security advisories access; alerts with Azure Policy.",
      say: `Here's Microsoft's starting point. Microsoft Learn publishes Resource Graph sample queries for Service Health: all active events, health advisories, upcoming retirements and planned maintenance. A second page gives the impacted-resources query. Reader on a subscription is enough to see its events, but a security advisory's sensitive fields and its impacted resources need Service Health Security Reader; Reader and Monitoring Reader can't see them. And for alerting between collections, Learn names a built-in policy that creates the Service Health alert rule in every subscription, with a remediation task for the ones that already exist.`,
      detail: `Learn publishes Resource Graph sample queries for Service Health: all active events, health advisories (whose mitigation time is the advisory's end), upcoming retirements (health advisories with EventSubType Retirement) and planned maintenance, each with links to the Azure portal and the Azure Government portal. A second page gives the impacted-resources query, which splits the tracking ID out of each impacted resource's ID. Reader on a subscription is enough to see its Service Health events. The sensitive fields of a security advisory, and its impacted resources, need Service Health Security Reader (or a role with the three actions it holds); Reader and Monitoring Reader can't see them. For alerting between collections, Learn's Deploy Service Health alerts at scale using Azure Policy names a built-in definition, Configure subscriptions to enable Service Health Monitoring Alert Rules, assigned at a management group or subscription, with a remediation task so existing subscriptions get the alert rule too.`,
      cite: ["pn01-arg-samples", "pn01-arg-impacted", "pn01-sub-tenant", "pn01-sec-elevated", "pn01-policy"],
      ref: "“Start with Microsoft's documentation” — “What Microsoft gives you”",
