      say: `Lab 1 needs only PowerShell 7 with Pester, working in the kit's folder, against two weeks of fictional notices from every provider. No tenant. Step 1 lists what Azure needs: this is what a reviewer reads before granting anything. Two calls, each needing Reader on each subscription in scope, each linked to the Learn page that says so. Step 2 prints the kit's events query. Compare it with Learn's all-active sample: the same filter, with the retirement sample's subtype added, the times converted, and named columns projected and ordered.`,
      detail: `You need PowerShell 7.1 or later with Pester 5. Work in examples/provider-notices. The fixtures are two weeks of fictional notices from every provider, tests/fixtures/day1 and day2, and tests/fixtures/settings.lab.json names fictional subscriptions in AzureCloud. Step 1, list what Azure needs: Import-Module ./powershell/ProviderNotices/ProviderNotices.psm1; Get-PnRequiredPermission -Provider azure | Format-List. Two calls, each needing Reader on each subscription in scope, with Service Health Security Reader named as the elevated role for security advisories (the Elevated lines are left out of the slide's first panel; the Who slide shows them). Step 2, read the kit's events query: Get-PnAzureQuery -Name events. Compare it with Learn's all-active sample: the same filter, with the retirement sample's EventSubType added and the times converted.`,
