      detail: `Step 5, read the retirement in full: (Read-PnJson -Path out/azure/notices.json).notices | Where-Object { $_.kind -eq 'retirement' } | ForEach-Object { [pscustomobject]$_ } | Format-List noticeId, windowStart, windowEnd, actionRequiredBy, actionBasis, resources, sourceUrl, fingerprint. noticeId azure:RT5J-6KL; windowStart 2026-09-30, windowEnd and actionRequiredBy 2027-09-30; actionBasis: rule: Azure retirement (HealthAdvisory, EventSubType Retirement); due at the advisory end time; resources: a public IP address in a fictional subscription (left out of the slide); sourceUrl on management.azure.com; and the fingerprint. Step 6: ./Invoke-PnCollect.ps1 ... -AsOf 2026-11-10T12:00:00Z -OutputPath out/azure-again, then compare the two runs' fingerprints with Compare-Object. A second read changes firstSeen in the run but no notice's fingerprint, so the router will see nothing new. The last line is Fingerprints that differ: 0. (The repeated summary table is left out of the slide.)`,
